{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_2845c1b030fe6d60\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_2845c1b030fe6d60/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Majority threshold for incorrect dates and key facts\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_4c0f46ab95a5321f30ddaa81\", \"member_b193085c828797658e0da615\", \"member_fa59c4a67b9437de29c74005\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether an incorrect date counts as major.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether an inaccurate key fact warrants a major grade even when tone is fine, and asks how to handle the task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the incorrect date on RP-3656 counts as major.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor says the wrong date changes which event happened first and considers that central.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the RP-3656 thread, a tutor says the wrong date changes which event happened first and explains that the same wrong year can be minor in background context and major in a chronology task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"For the tutor's example, the team lead instructs that a factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion and a nonessential background-date slip is minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions classify a factual error as major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on, and a nonessential background error without that effect as minor; the current FAQ gives the same distinction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"One QA tutor's question has no answer in its provided thread, while the QA tutor asking about RP-3656 receives a tutor's contextual explanation but no definitive classification of the task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors and a tutor ask when incorrect dates or key facts count as major factual errors.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance defines the threshold, but one QA tutor's question remains unanswered and the other has only a tutor's contextual explanation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead answered the tutor's question within that thread: a factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion, while a nonessential background-date slip is minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"For RP-3656, a tutor says the wrong date changes the event order and explains that the same wrong year can be minor in background context but major in a chronology task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a reminder explaining that incorrect dates and key facts are graded by their effect on the central conclusion or actionable answer. Draft to copy: Reminder for date and key-fact reviews: an incorrect fact is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on. A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n\\nApply that distinction to the role the date or fact plays in the answer, rather than treating every incorrect date as automatically major. This follows the current factual-error instructions and FAQ; it does not introduce a new grading threshold. Scope: This reminder restates the factual-error threshold; it does not assign a final grade to either QA tutor's example.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current instructions and FAQ already supply the same threshold. A reminder addresses the remaining grading questions without introducing a new rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Two QA tutors' date-grading questions remain unanswered or only partly answered, despite an applicable factual-error rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_4c0f46ab95a5321f30ddaa81\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_4c0f46ab95a5321f30ddaa81 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks whether the date error is major; the provided thread contains no reply.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b193085c828797658e0da615\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b193085c828797658e0da615 is RESOLVED_IN_THREAD: The team lead answers the tutor's handling question with a threshold explicitly scoped to that example.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_fa59c4a67b9437de29c74005\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_fa59c4a67b9437de29c74005 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: A tutor explains why the event order matters and how context can change the grade, but does not definitively classify RP-3656 for the QA tutor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: Repeated uncertainty concerns the distinction between major and minor factual defects, which can affect grading consistency. The messages do not establish broader disruption or incorrect submitted labels.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[0]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\\\": Two QA tutors and a tutor ask how incorrect dates or key facts should be graded, showing repeated uncertainty about the same consequential grading distinction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790857505.000025\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4c0f46ab95a5321f30ddaa81\", \"thread_id\": \"1790857505.000025\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T12:25:05.000025Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Does this incorrect date count as major?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877012.001300\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b193085c828797658e0da615\", \"thread_id\": \"1790877012.001300\", \"author_id\": \"U003\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:50:12.001300Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U003\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"[Task review]\\nIssue: Is the key fact being inaccurate enough to trigger major even if tone is fine?\\nQuestion: what is the correct handling for this task?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877065.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b193085c828797658e0da615\", \"thread_id\": \"1790877012.001300\", \"author_id\": \"U012\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:51:05.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U003\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thinking_face\", \"users\": [\"U011\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"The wrong date changes which event happened first; that seems central.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790877109.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b193085c828797658e0da615\", \"thread_id\": \"1790877012.001300\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:51:49.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U003\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"For this example, a factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion; a nonessential background-date slip is minor.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893656.000022\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_fa59c4a67b9437de29c74005\", \"thread_id\": \"1790893656.000022\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:27:36.000022Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Does this incorrect date count as major? (task ref RP-3656)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790893706.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_fa59c4a67b9437de29c74005\", \"thread_id\": \"1790893656.000022\", \"author_id\": \"U004\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:28:26.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thinking_face\", \"users\": [\"U013\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"The wrong date changes which event happened first; that seems central. The same wrong year can be minor in background context and major in a chronology task.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-16T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_14): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nPreference batch 14 calibration: choose a tie when neither answer offers a meaningful quality advantage. If choosing A or B, identify the user-facing benefit rather than saying only that it sounds nicer. Keep material factual or instruction-following defects separate. Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review. This message clarifies the existing criterion; it does not create a new numerical threshold.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction adherence versus accuracy\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction adherence versus accuracy\\nScore these dimensions separately. An explicit required output structure, such